## Why This Is Asked
Addresses detection/containment of DNS exfiltration in multi-cloud, a gap in the existing questions.

## Key Concepts
- DNS exfiltration patterns (long queries, high entropy)
- Cross‑cloud log sources (AWS Route 53 Resolver logs, IBM DNS, Cloudflare Gateway logs)
- SIEM correlation (Splunk/QRadar)
- Containment actions (Cloudflare Gateway blocking, firewall rules) and IR coordination

## Code Example
```javascript
function dnsExfiltrationDetected(log) {
  const longQuery = log.query.length > 60;
  const highEntropy = /[A-Za-z0-9+/]{60,}/.test(log.query);
  const unusualTLD = /\.(xyz|top|icu|cc)$/i.test(log.domain);
  return longQuery && highEntropy && unusualTLD;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you tune FP/FN rates across clouds?
- How would you test the IR playbook without impacting business?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical CISSP logging, monitoring, and incident-response planning for distributed data platforms at a beginner level.

## Key Concepts
- Access control and RBAC
- Logging and monitoring
- Log integrity and tamper-evidence
- SIEM and alerting
- Incident tabletop and validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple log entry hash for integrity (illustrative)
const crypto = require('crypto');
function hashLog(entry, key){
  const h = crypto.createHash('sha256');
  h.update(JSON.stringify(entry));
  h.update(key);
  return h.digest('hex');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would data-residency rules affect log storage and access?
- What retention, deletion, and privacy controls would you implement for analytics logs?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes crypto governance at scale, bridging cloud-native KMS with on-prem HSMs, PKI, and policy-driven agility. It tests risk framing, regulatory considerations, and incident response readiness.

## Key Concepts
- Crypto agility and policy-driven key selection
- HSMs, PKI, certificate management
- Key lifecycle, rotation, retirement
- Access control, least privilege, and audits
- Post-quantum readiness and algorithm agility

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: select allowed algorithm per policy
const policy = getCryptoPolicy();
function selectAlgorithm(payload){
  for (const a of policy.allowedAlgorithms){
    if (canUse(a, payload)) return a;
  }
  throw new Error('No suitable algorithm available');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate crypto policy changes without interrupting live traffic?
- What are trade-offs between cloud KMS and on-prem HSMs for encryption at rest vs in transit in high-load fintech workflows?
